    "id": "p13-g49-51-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "49",
    "prompt": "Find the coefficient of the term indicated in the following expansions.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p13-g49-51-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$(2-x+3x^2)(1+4x)^4$; term indicated: $x^3$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$464$.",
          "worked": "Match the polynomial terms with powers three, two and one in the binomial expansion. Let $C$ be the required coefficient.\n$$\\begin{align*}C&=2\\binom{4}{3}4^3-\\binom{4}{2}4^2+3\\binom{4}{1}4\\\\C&=512-96+48\\\\C&=464\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-g49-51-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$(3+2x-x^2)(5-x)^5$; term indicated: $x^4$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-1675$.",
          "worked": "Match the polynomial terms with powers four, three and two in the binomial expansion. Let $C$ be the required coefficient.\n$$\\begin{align*}C&=3\\binom{5}{4}5(-1)^4+2\\binom{5}{3}5^2(-1)^3-\\binom{5}{2}5^3(-1)^2\\\\C&=75-500-1250\\\\C&=-1675\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-g49-51-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$(1-3x+2x^2)(2+x)^6$; term indicated: $x^5$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$152$.",
          "worked": "Match the polynomial terms with powers five, four and three in the binomial expansion. Let $C$ be the required coefficient.\n$$\\begin{align*}C&=\\binom{6}{5}2-3\\binom{6}{4}2^2+2\\binom{6}{3}2^3\\\\C&=12-180+320\\\\C&=152\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      }
    ]
